  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Igua - CEDAE Concession Bloco 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project consists of the design, construction, operation and maintenance of Block 2 of the Concession for the water distribution, sewage collection and treatment systems in the municipalities of Rio de Janeiro, Paty do Alferes and Miguel Pereira in the State of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil. In the latter two municipalities, Igu&#xE1; Rio de Janeiro will also be responsible for water collection and treatment. The aim, in addition to universal water distribution, is to achieve 90% sewage collection and treatment for approximately 1.2 million people. The financial plan consists of an IDB Invest loan of up to R$1 billion, with a term of up to 20 years.</narrative>
  </description>
